EXT. SUNNYBROOK PETTING ZOO - DAY

Hay bales. A painted red barn. A banner reads HAPPY 7TH BIRTHDAY, TEDDY! Beneath it, a crowd of parents with phones.

A BIRTHDAY CLOWN, 40s, in an orange wig and enormous shoes, wrestles a bundle of balloon animals. A goat watches him with great interest.

MRS. PRIYANKA DESHMUKH, 40s, blazer, lanyard, a party planner with a tight smile, marches over with a clipboard.

TEDDY, 7, birthday boy, paper crown crooked, stands at the pen. He holds a carrot out to the goat. He is very serious.

DOLORES SWAN, 50s, the zookeeper, in rubber boots and a faded cap, leans on a rake and stares at the clown with wary eyes.

PRIYANKA
You're ten minutes late.

CLOWN
Traffic. Also the goat ate my map.

PRIYANKA
You're a clown. You don't need a map.

CLOWN
I'm a fully qualified clown, ma'am. I have a certificate.

DOLORES
He's got a certificate.

PRIYANKA
Do you have a name, certificate?

CLOWN
Giggles.

PRIYANKA
Your real name.

CLOWN
(lowering his voice)
Gerald.

DOLORES
Gerald, that goat has been staring at you for five minutes. He doesn't like clowns.

GERALD
Why not?

DOLORES
Last clown was a bad time.

The goat lowers its head. Gerald backs away. The goat steps forward. Gerald trips over his shoe, grabs a balloon sword from his belt, thrusts it like a rapier. The sword POPS. The goat CHARGES.

Gerald bolts across the yard, wig flying, shoes flapping. Priyanka drops the clipboard. Dolores drops the rake and sprints after the goat, shouting. Teddy bursts into laughter and runs after all of them, crown bouncing. The parents' phones come up like a field of tiny cameras.

GERALD (CONT'D)
(over his shoulder)
Is that a good goat?!

DOLORES
That's a goat!

Gerald vaults a hay bale and lands face-first in the pen. The goat skids to a stop. Sniffs his wig. Eats it.

Silence. Then applause.

TEDDY
Best birthday ever!

Gerald lies in the straw, hairless, beaming.
